  "limits": [
    "Shared-basis fitting accepts 1 to 32 open oriented sources with 2 to 32 ordered contacts, degree at most 16, at most 128 controls per source and 2048 total source controls. At least four spans per interval and at most 125 spans total give at most 128 fitted controls. Existing normalized common-sign weight and continuity restrictions apply.",
    "Fit distance is a sampled upper estimate in the private frame, not a continuous original-image certificate or a world-restoration rounding bound. Exact restored contact proofs qualify discrete positions only. Complete original-image admission is a separate downstream requirement and all twelve regression/diagnostic originals pass at 1e-6.",
    "The smooth quintic arc-length clock is an independent proposal policy. Its 25 returned closest-point comparisons still fail the requested 1e-6 Rhino interior tolerance. C2 basis continuity and complete original-image bounds do not qualify injectivity, topology, symmetric distance or Rhino parity.",
    "Both native correction stages are bounded. Projection failures, inadequate fixed bases, collapsed clocks, invalid inputs and inconclusive proofs can reject valid geometry; no unchecked candidate is returned.",
    "SMLib, SM_API and the adapter use AddressSanitizer and frame pointers. Rust and separately bundled dependencies are not separately instrumented. Leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks are disabled. No performance qualification is claimed."
  ],
